§ `Fixtures (no provision)`

`no evidence holidays` MEANS EMPTY

-- An agreement for 9 Evidence St with the lessor L (who granted it), rent a fixed amount, nothing set out,
-- no notice under s 70A, delivery of possession on the day it terminated (if it has).
GIVEN nme IS A STRING
      tns IS A LIST OF STRING
      kd  IS A `Kind of tenancy`
      st  IS A NUMBER
      ex  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      wr  IS A NUMBER
      te  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`evidence agreement` nme `with` tns `,` kd `from day` st `, expiry` ex `, at weekly rent` wr `, terminated` te MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS nme
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS tns
        `premises`                                       IS "9 Evidence St"
        `kind`                                           IS kd
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS st
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS st
        `expiry day`                                     IS ex
        `weekly rent`                                    IS wr
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS te
        `terminated on`                                  IS te
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

-- The same, for a fixed term with the notices under s 70A given.
GIVEN nme IS A STRING
      st  IS A NUMBER
      ex  IS A NUMBER
      ns  IS A LIST OF `Notice under s 70A`
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`evidence fixed term` nme `from day` st `to day` ex `with the notices under s 70A` ns MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS nme
        `lessor`                                         IS "L"
        `granted by`                                     IS "L"
        `tenants`                                        IS LIST "T1"
        `premises`                                       IS "9 Evidence St"
        `kind`                                           IS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS st
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS st
        `expiry day`                                     IS JUST ex
        `weekly rent`                                    IS 500
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS ns
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS NOTHING
        `terminated on`                                  IS NOTHING
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

GIVEN nm IS A STRING, g IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rent variation`
`an evidence increase under s 30 of` nm `noticed on day` g `, taking effect on day` e `, to` r MEANS
    `Rent variation` WITH `agreement` IS nm, `under` IS `section 30`, `notice given on` IS g, `took effect on` IS e, `weekly rent from then` IS r

GIVEN as IS A LIST OF `Residential tenancy agreement`
      vs IS A LIST OF `Rent variation`
GIVETH A `Rent history`
`the evidence history of` as `with` vs MEANS `Rent history` WITH `agreements` IS as, `variations` IS vs

GIVEN g IS A NUMBER, pd IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice under s 64`
`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` g `for possession on day` pd MEANS
    `Notice under s 64` WITH `given on` IS g, `received by the tenant on` IS g, `possession day specified` IS pd

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the evidence count of` xs MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS (`the evidence count of` rest)

§ `L-04 -- an agreement the parties replace while the tenant stays does not end (s 60(1))`

-- W1: periodic from 1 January 2025 at $500. On 30 June 2026 the parties agree to replace it with W2, a fixed
-- term from 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 at $600, and the tenant stays. No circumstance in s 60(1) ends W1, so
-- both are in force on 1 September 2026, at different rents.
`W1` MEANS `evidence agreement` "W1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, terminated` NOTHING
`W2` MEANS `evidence agreement` "W2" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `a tenancy for a fixed term` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` (JUST (`day number` 2027 6 30)) `, at weekly rent` 600 `, terminated` NOTHING
`W history` MEANS `the evidence history of` (LIST `W1`, `W2`) `with` EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` (`an agreement to terminate, the tenant staying in possession` (`day number` 2026 6 30)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 -- day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `falls in the tenancy period of` `W1`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `falls in the tenancy period of` `W2`
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `W1` `on day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `, given` `W history` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `W2` `on day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `, given` `W history` EQUALS 600
-- W2 continues nothing (s 31B(2)(c)): W1's term has not ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `W2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `W1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
-- During W2's fixed term the lessor may end W1, still in force and periodic, by notice without a ground
-- (60 clear days, 1 September to 1 November 2026); under W2 the same notice is no notice (s 64(5)).
#ASSERT `s 64 -- the notice` (`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `for possession on day` (`day number` 2026 11 1)) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `W1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64 -- the notice` (`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` (`day number` 2026 9 1) `for possession on day` (`day number` 2026 11 1)) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `W2` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)

§ `L-05 -- a new tenant: a rent set at will and a fresh 12 months, after an ending without a ground`

-- Z1: periodic from 1 January 2025 at $500, increased under s 30 to $550 from 1 January 2026. On 1 March 2026
-- the lessor gives notice without a ground for 1 May 2026, and the tenant leaves that day. Z2: from 2 May 2026
-- the lessor lets the premises to a new tenant, T9, at $700.
`Z1` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Z1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 5 1))
`Z2` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Z2" `with` (LIST "T9") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2026 5 2) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 700 `, terminated` NOTHING
`Z history` MEANS `the evidence history of` (LIST `Z1`, `Z2`) `with` (LIST (`an evidence increase under s 30 of` "Z1" `noticed on day` (`day number` 2025 10 1) `, taking effect on day` (`day number` 2026 1 1) `, to` 550))

#ASSERT `s 64 -- the notice` (`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for possession on day` (`day number` 2026 5 1)) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `Z1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT `s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` (`a notice of termination under the Act, then vacant possession (s 60(1)(a)(i))` (`day number` 2026 5 1) (`day number` 2026 5 1)) EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `Z2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `Z1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
-- On either reading of FK-01 the $700 is not limited: Z2 continues nothing.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `Z2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `Z history` `and the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
#ASSERT NOT (`FK-01 reading B -- s 30(1) -- the rent fixed by` `Z2` `is an increase otherwise than under the section, given` `Z history` `and the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
#ASSERT `the weekly rent payable under` `Z2` `on day` (`day number` 2026 5 2) `, given` `Z history` EQUALS 700
-- Under Z1 itself the rent could not have risen to $700 before 1 January 2027 (s 30(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30 -- the notice` (`a s 30 notice under` "Z1" `given on day` (`day number` 2026 3 1) `for weekly rent` 700 `from day` (`day number` 2026 5 2)) `increases the rent under` `Z1` `from the day it specifies, given` `Z history` `and the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)

§ `L-07 -- s 31B(3)(b) and a change between one tenant and co-tenants`

-- The literal words of s 31B(3)(b), for evidence only (not a reading in the fork register: the encoding
-- counts any tenant in common, without recording a fork). "The tenant ... is the same under both agreements"
-- is read as speaking of an agreement with one tenant (s 3 "party" (a)(ii)) on each side, and "at least 1
-- co-tenant ... is the same under both agreements" of agreements with co-tenants (s 3 "party" (a)(iii)) on
-- each side.
GIVEN c IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, e IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `L-07 literal reading -- s 31B(3)(b) holds for` c `and` e IF
        (    (`the evidence count of` (c's `tenants`) EQUALS 1)
         AND (`the evidence count of` (e's `tenants`) EQUALS 1)
         AND (`some member of` (c's `tenants`) `is among` (e's `tenants`)))
    OR  (    (`the evidence count of` (c's `tenants`) AT LEAST 2)
         AND (`the evidence count of` (e's `tenants`) AT LEAST 2)
         AND (`some member of` (c's `tenants`) `is among` (e's `tenants`)))

-- Y1: T1 alone, periodic from 1 January 2025, ended 30 June 2026 with vacant possession. Y2: T1 and T2 as
-- co-tenants from 1 July 2026. Y3: T1 and T2, periodic from 1 January 2025, ended 30 June 2026. Y4: T2 alone
-- from 1 July 2026.
`Y1` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Y1" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`Y2` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Y2" `with` (LIST "T1", "T2") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, terminated` NOTHING
`Y3` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Y3" `with` (LIST "T1", "T2") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 500 `, terminated` (JUST (`day number` 2026 6 30))
`Y4` MEANS `evidence agreement` "Y4" `with` (LIST "T2") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, terminated` NOTHING

-- The encoding: any tenant in common makes the same parties, so both are continuations.
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `Y2` `is taken to be a continuation of` `Y1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT `s 31B(2) -- the agreement` `Y4` `is taken to be a continuation of` `Y3` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
-- The literal words: neither limb is met in either direction.
#ASSERT NOT (`L-07 literal reading -- s 31B(3)(b) holds for` `Y2` `and` `Y1`)
#ASSERT NOT (`L-07 literal reading -- s 31B(3)(b) holds for` `Y4` `and` `Y3`)
-- Where the line-up does not change between one tenant and co-tenants, the two agree.
#ASSERT `L-07 literal reading -- s 31B(3)(b) holds for` (`evidence agreement` "Y5" `with` (LIST "T1") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, terminated` NOTHING) `and` `Y1`
#ASSERT `L-07 literal reading -- s 31B(3)(b) holds for` (`evidence agreement` "Y6" `with` (LIST "T2", "T3") `,` `a periodic tenancy` `from day` (`day number` 2026 7 1) `, expiry` NOTHING `, at weekly rent` 620 `, terminated` NOTHING) `and` `Y3`

§ `L-24 -- a notice under s 70A given after s 76C has continued the agreement as a periodic tenancy`

-- V1: a fixed term for 2025 at $500, nothing set out and no notice under s 70A, so from 1 January 2026 it
-- continues as a periodic tenancy (s 76C). On Monday 2 March 2026 the lessor gives a notice under s 70A for
-- possession on 1 April 2026, 30 days later. V1N is V1 with that notice.
`V1` MEANS `evidence fixed term` "V1" `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `to day` (`day number` 2025 12 31) `with the notices under s 70A` EMPTY
`V1's notice of 2 March 2026` MEANS `Notice under s 70A` WITH `given by` IS `the lessor`, `given on` IS `day number` 2026 3 2, `possession day specified` IS `day number` 2026 4 1
`V1N` MEANS `evidence fixed term` "V1" `from day` (`day number` 2025 1 1) `to day` (`day number` 2025 12 31) `with the notices under s 70A` (LIST `V1's notice of 2 March 2026`)

#ASSERT `s 76C(2) -- the first day of the periodic tenancy continuing` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 1 1)
-- The encoding accepts the notice: s 70A(1), (3) and (4) say nothing of when it is given.
#ASSERT `s 70A -- the notice` `V1's notice of 2 March 2026` `is a notice under the section for` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT `s 70A -- the day the term of` `V1N` `ends under the section, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 4 1)
-- and with it the fixed term now runs to 1 April 2026, and the periodic tenancy begins only after it:
#ASSERT `the last day of the fixed term of` `V1N` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 76C(2) -- the first day of the periodic tenancy continuing` `V1N` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays` EQUALS JUST (`day number` 2026 4 2)
-- 15 February 2026, when the agreement was periodic, is now "during the currency of the fixed term", so an
-- increase that took effect that day (nothing set out) is barred by s 30(2)(a) after the event.
#ASSERT NOT (`is day` (`day number` 2026 2 15) `during the currency of the fixed term of` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
#ASSERT `is day` (`day number` 2026 2 15) `during the currency of the fixed term of` `V1N` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(a) -- the right to increase is exercisable for` (`a s 30 notice under` "V1" `given on day` (`day number` 2025 12 1) `for weekly rent` 540 `from day` (`day number` 2026 2 15)) `under` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(2)(a) -- the right to increase is exercisable for` (`a s 30 notice under` "V1" `given on day` (`day number` 2025 12 1) `for weekly rent` 540 `from day` (`day number` 2026 2 15)) `under` `V1N` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
-- The same day, a notice without a ground needs 60 clear days: possession on 1 April fails, 2 May is enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64 -- the notice` (`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` (`day number` 2026 3 2) `for possession on day` (`day number` 2026 4 1)) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`)
#ASSERT `s 64 -- the notice` (`an evidence s 64 notice given on day` (`day number` 2026 3 2) `for possession on day` (`day number` 2026 5 2)) `is a notice of termination under the section for` `V1` `, given the holidays` `no evidence holidays`

